WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  this boeing  747-300 did belong to the iranian cargo  company mahan air  last year they sold it to the venezuelan  firm empress or cargo  the us says it did not authorize that  transaction which broke its export  control laws they want the plane  confiscated  iran denies the accusations while  venezuela wants the aircraft back  the plane that was carrying out a  fundamental humanitarian mission for  venezuela has been kidnapped by  argentina they've robbed us on the  orders of an imperialist court in the  united states  venezuela raises its voice in protest  and calls for unity with the honest  people of argentina  an argentine judge released 12 of the 19  crew members seven remain three  venezuelans and four iranians among them  the pilot colombrissa gassemi  the us believes he belongs to the cudd's  force of iran's revolutionary guard  sanctioned by the us but not argentina  as a terror organization  it's a case shrouded in confusion and  counter claims  what we do know for now is that the  boeing 747 belonging to the venezuelan  cargo company empressor has been  impounded here at buenos aires's assaisa  airport for two months  israel has praised the argentine  authorities for its action suggesting at  least some of the crew might be involved  in smuggling weapons  argentina was in the 1990s the victim of  two attacks it said iran was involved in  one on the israeli embassy and one on a  jewish cultural center  no one's been brought to justice for  either bombing and jewish organizations  in argentina one of possible future  attacks  they want the plane and its crew  investigated  if we see a link i don't know if there's  a link with the attacks in 1992 and 1994  but it could be a preparatory mission  for an attack in argentina for somewhere  else in latin america  the lawyer acting for the detained pilot  told al jazeera the case was political  as well as legal involved a lot of  paperwork and is unlikely to be resolved  anytime soon  meanwhile the plane remains firmly on  the ground  daniel schweiner al-jazeera buenos aires

